{{Quote|An attack on Taanab—though on the Perlemian Trade Route—would earn the dissidents more condemnation than praise, as Taanab's agricultural projects feed billions in the Mid and Outer Rim.|Vice Admiral Dodd Rancit explains why it is unlikely that the ''[[Carrion Spike]]'' will target Taanab despite its placement on the Perlemian Trade Route|<ref name="Trkn" />}}
The '''Perlemian Trade Route''' was a [[super-hyperroute]]<ref name="BMF 48">{{BuildFalconCite|48|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref> which included the [[planet]]s [[Felucia]]<ref name="GD" /> and [[Taanab]].<ref name="Trkn" /> During the [[Clone Wars]], thanks to a [[Galactic Republic]] in the [[Battle of Murkhana]], the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]]'s [[Shadowfeed]]s were unable to reach the planets across the Perlemian Trade Route.<ref name="OF84">{{GermanFanCite|84|Database}}</ref>

When considering potential targets for the stolen [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[corvette]] ''[[Carrion Spike]]'', [[Vice Admiral]] [[Dodd Rancit]] ruled out Taanab as being at risk despite its placement on the trade route, as the planet supplied [[Foodstuff|food]] to many other planets.<ref name="Trkn" />

The [[Sakavian]] fisherman Skoova Stev found himself marooned in deep space along the Perlemian Trade Route, after being jettisoned in an escape pod by his former captain, the [[Besalisk]] [[Wan'yek Whett]]. He was later rescued by a passing [[Purrgil]].<ref name="Survivor">''[[Star Wars Jedi: Survivor]]''</ref>

